"Commercial Revenue" means the gross revenue, before deductions other than refunds and taxes collected on behalf of a government, earned by you and your Affiliates from products or services that incorporate the Software, depend on the Software, or use the Software as a material part of their delivery.

If revenue attributable to the Commercial Use cannot reasonably be separated from other revenue, Commercial Revenue means the gross revenue of the business operation in which the Software is used.

"Affiliate" means an entity that controls, is controlled by, or is under common control with you. "Control" means the direct or indirect power to direct management or policies, whether through ownership, contract, or otherwise.

Amounts received in currencies other than Australian dollars must be converted to Australian dollars using a reasonable published market exchange rate for the relevant accounting period.

